<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Church of Scotland</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1560">1560</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as The Kirk, the Kirk</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Church of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, known as the Kirk, is Scotland's national church, Presbyterian in government and Reformed in doctrine. It emerged from the Scottish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> of 1560 led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-knox">John Knox</a> and, after long conflict with the Stuart kings over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a>, was confirmed as Presbyterian in 1690. Its position was guaranteed by the Treaty of Union in 1707, and it is governed by a General Assembly rather than bishops.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/church-of-scotland.jpg" alt="Church of Scotland" width="320" height="460" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kaihsu · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NecTamenConsumebatur.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
